It sounds like the synopsis

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:10.850
for an episode of Law &amp; Order SVU.

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:13.610
A billionaire financier is
arrested for human trafficking

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:16.110
in New York after the
FBI uncovers evidence

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.260
that he lured underage girls to his house

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:20.070
where they were molested, assaulted,

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:23.040
and worse by the billionaire,
and his famous pals.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.380
The public is shocked that the
billionaire was investigated

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.540
for the same conduct 15 years ago,

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.510
and got away with everything.

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:31.530
The billionaire happens to
have a little black book

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.270
containing the contact
information for those

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:35.050
powerful people in America,

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.610
including former, and current presidents.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:40.130
This is not in fact an episode of SVU.

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:41.540
This is real life.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.690
Let's look into the multiple prosecutions

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:44.925
of Jeffrey Epstein.

00:00:44.925 --> 00:00:48.950
(upbeat jaunty jingle)

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:51.640
Hey, legal eagles, it's
time to think like a lawyer,

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.830
and today we are gonna
talk about Jeffrey Epstein,

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:58.690
who is under indictment again
for potential sex trafficking.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:01.560
Jeffrey Epstein is a billionaire
financier who is friends,

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.880
and associates with several rich,

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.840
and powerful people including
President Donald Trump,

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.832
who once called Epstein, a quote,

00:01:07.832 --> 00:01:10.047
"terrific guy who likes
beautiful women as much as I do,

00:01:10.047 --> 00:01:12.490
"and many of them are
on the younger side."

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:15.510
Epstein has been investigated
repeatedly for trafficking

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:18.680
children who were then forced
to have sex with Epstein,

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.270
and his famous friends.

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:22.630
There's evidence that the
president may have known about,

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:25.710
or have seen red flags
associated with Epstein,

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:29.140
and that president Trump's
now former labor secretary

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:31.240
helped cover up some of these crimes.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.350
Now before I go too much further,

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:35.720
a quick disclaimer about
indictments versus convictions.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:39.130
It is far too easy to assume
that someone who is indicted

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:42.240
of a crime is guilty of
the underlying offense.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.870
Too often that is not the case,

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:48.380
and everyone in America is
entitled to a fair hearing,

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:50.880
so we should look at facts
as they are disclosed

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.340
to the public with a grain
of salt, and with skepticism.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:57.280
Here, there is both a pending indictment

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.000
as well as a plea deal
that covered at least

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.400
some of this alleged conduct.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.970
So there's less of a potential issue

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:06.120
in this particular case,

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.340
because some of the facts
have been admitted to,

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.990
but it's still important to recognize

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:12.560
that people who have been
indicted are not guilty

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.650
until proven beyond a reasonable
doubt in a court of law.

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:16.570
So with that understanding,

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:20.070
let's first define what we
mean by human sex trafficking.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.826
The Justice for Victims of
Trafficking Act of 2015,

00:02:22.826 --> 00:02:26.780
or JTA defines sex
trafficking as recruiting,

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:30.130
harboring, transporting,
providing, obtaining, patronizing,

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:32.760
or soliciting of an individual
through the means of force,

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.190
fraud, or coercion for the
purpose of commercial sex.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:38.180
However, it is not necessary
to demonstrate force,

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:40.500
fraud, or coercion in
sex trafficking cases

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.770
involving children under the age of 18.

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:46.440
The term commercial sex act
is defined as any sex act

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.870
on account of which
anything of value is given,

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:50.950
or received by any person.

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:54.290
It is illegal to have sex with
someone who is under-aged.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.300
I probably don't need to explain that,

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.180
but in this day,

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.060
and age it's better to be safe than sorry.

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:01.300
So keep that in mind when
you hear some of the offenses

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:04.690
that refer to allegations of consent.

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:06.920
Children cannot consent to the acts

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.540
that Epstein has allegedly committed.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:10.710
So the allegations,

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:14.090
and admissions relevant here
are broken up into two phases.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:16.040
The first is in the early 2000s.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:17.950
In 2005 a 14 year old girl,

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:20.691
and her parents told Palm Beach,
Florida police detectives,

00:03:20.691 --> 00:03:24.580
that Jeffrey Epstein had paid
her, and a classmate for sex.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:25.870
The Palm Beach Police Department

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:27.170
started investigating Epstein

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:29.660
for soliciting underage
girls for prostitution.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:31.810
They alleged that
Epstein's two assistants,

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:35.310
Haley Robson, and Sarah Kellen
would recruit teenage girls

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:37.290
to give Epstein massages in the bedroom

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.920
of his Palm Beach mansion.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:40.050
Once inside the house,

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:41.950
Epstein would order the
girls to strip naked,

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.720
and he would assault them
during, and after the massage.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:46.770
The Palm Beach Police did trash pulls

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:48.260
where they went through his garbage,

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:49.870
and found trash with the girl's names,

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.400
and cell phone numbers on it.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.350
Epstein's assistant actually telephoned

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.830
one of the victims while
she was talking to police.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.394
As the police investigation continued,

00:03:57.394 --> 00:03:59.330
more victims were identified.

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:02.470
The police promptly issued
a probable cause affidavit,

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:03.610
which normally is all that's needed

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:04.980
to arrest a person in Florida,

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.998
but in a highly unusual move,

00:04:06.998 --> 00:04:08.430
the district attorney's office

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:10.620
referred the charges to
a grand jury instead.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.580
The local prosecutors
only presented evidence

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:14.490
that Epstein assaulted one of the girls,

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:16.500
and they failed to ask
the jury to indict Epstein

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:18.090
for having sex with a minor.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.670
Instead, Epstein was indicted

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:21.600
for solicitation of prostitution,

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.210
which is a much less serious charge.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:27.080
Epstein's legal team swooped
in to negotiate a plea deal

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.030
that would have allowed Epstein

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:30.350
to enter into a pretrial
diversion program,

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:31.970
and served no jail time.

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:34.630
In other words, the local
prosecutors were being pressured

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:36.800
to just give Epstein a slap on the wrist.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.520
The Palm Beach police were not
happy with this negotiation,

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:41.410
and they referred the case to the FBI,

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:43.755
which opened a case file
on Epstein for activities

00:04:43.755 --> 00:04:47.100
with underage victims in Florida,
New York, and New Mexico.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:50.000
A 53 page federal indictment was prepared,

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.770
but not filed with the
Florida district court.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.060
At the same time,

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.040
Epstein's lawyers were
negotiating a plea deal

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:58.020
with the U.S. attorney in Miami,

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.180
Alex Acosta,

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:01.980
who later became president
Trump's labor secretary.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:02.813
At the time,

00:05:02.813 --> 00:05:04.890
Epstein's lawyers
included Alan Dershowitz,

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:07.400
and Ken Star among other
legal stall boards.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.820
Dershowitz is most famous
for defending OJ Simpson.

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:12.220
While Star was the independent prosecutor

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:13.440
who investigated Bill Clinton

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.370
for having an affair with Monica Lewinsky.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:16.930
Later Star became president,

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:18.890
and chancellor at Baylor University.

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:20.420
Allegedly during the negotiation,

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.800
Star was working overtime for Epstein.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.470
Star told Alex Acosta again,

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:26.330
the U.S. attorney for Miami at the time,

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:27.670
that his client would not agree

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:29.240
to being classified as a sex offender,

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:31.550
which is normally mandatory
for anyone convicted

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:32.690
of a sex offense.

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:35.240
Star also objected to an
addendum to the agreement

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:37.113
that said that the victims

00:05:37.113 --> 00:05:38.310
would be able to sue for compensation.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:40.460
Star worked his connections
in the Department of Justice

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:43.140
to request a review of the agreement.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:45.050
The review went on for more than a year,

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:47.633
and during this time the
FBI continued to investigate

00:05:47.633 --> 00:05:49.020
starting up more victims,

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:50.740
and more evidence against Epstein.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:53.320
The FBI's new allegations
included information showing

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:57.260
that Epstein preyed on runaways
as young as 13 years old,

00:05:57.260 --> 00:06:00.280
paying them for nude
massages that led to sex.

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:02.530
The investigation apparently
revealed how Epstein

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:05.470
preyed on poor children
using his assistance to find

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:08.520
vulnerable teen girls who they then paid

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.029
to recruit other teens.

00:06:10.029 --> 00:06:13.230
Of course, minors cannot
legally consent to sex.

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:14.063
All in all,

00:06:14.063 --> 00:06:17.260
investigators turned up at
least 80 under age victims.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:19.990
Importantly, prosecutors also
found that some of the girls

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:22.770
were given work with a
Manhattan modeling agency,

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:24.010
while they were also living

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:26.200
in an apartment owned by Epstein.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.020
While a new indictment was prepared,

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.718
prosecutors reported
that Epstein's lawyers

00:06:29.718 --> 00:06:32.320
had been harassing the victims.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.993
However, Acosta was firmly in
charge of the negotiations,

00:06:34.993 --> 00:06:36.764
and agreed to give Epstein

00:06:36.764 --> 00:06:40.550
what can only be called
the plea deal of a century.

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:42.893
So let's talk about this
non-prosecution agreement.

00:06:42.893 --> 00:06:45.340
Epstein pleaded guilty to a single count

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:46.990
of solicitation of prostitution,

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:49.380
and a single count of
prostitution with a minor

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:50.608
under the age of 18.

00:06:50.608 --> 00:06:53.460
The court sentenced him
to 18 months in jail,

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:56.250
and adjudicated him as a
convicted sex offender.

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:57.750
The agreement granted Epstein,

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:01.430
and incredibly his unindicted
co-conspirators immunity

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:02.740
from federal charges.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:04.330
This is unbelievably unusual.

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:07.720
You don't give pleased to
people that you haven't named

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:08.810
in an indictment.

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:10.520
The federal non-prosecution agreement

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:13.040
was also marked by other things
that were highly irregular,

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:14.570
and borderline unethical.

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:16.650
For example, Epstein's
somehow managed to remove

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:18.420
his computers from his main residence

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:20.970
before the FBI was able
to search the house.

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:22.155
Secondly, although subpoenas

00:07:22.155 --> 00:07:24.420
were prepared for the computer records,

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:26.760
law enforcement never
required Epstein to comply

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:28.140
with any of the subpoenas,

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:30.684
and finally, although
the plea negotiations

00:07:30.684 --> 00:07:32.900
typically include several
Department of Justice lawyers,

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:35.580
allegedly Acosta met
with Epstein's lawyers

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:38.280
one-on-one without any
backup from the DOJ.

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:40.110
The end result was a highly unusual,

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:43.120
some would say disastrous
non-prosecution agreement

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:45.640
that would only be made public
more than 10 years later.

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:47.290
In exchange for Epstein's guilty pleas

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:49.470
to Florida's criminal
solicitation charges,

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:51.420
the Department of Justice
agreed not to pursue

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:52.820
criminal charges against Epstein

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:54.750
for all of the other allegations.

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:57.090
Acosta used his authority
to lead prosecutors

00:07:57.090 --> 00:08:00.550
to drop all other investigations
into Epstein's conduct.

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:03.460
Further, it appears that Acosta
agree to hide the agreement

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:06.550
from the victims, and other
witnesses in this case.

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:08.614
He granted Epstein's,
unindicted co-conspirators,

00:08:08.614 --> 00:08:11.159
and employees blanket
immunity from prosecution.

00:08:11.159 --> 00:08:12.790
Some of these people were named,

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:14.511
and some were completely anonymous.

00:08:14.511 --> 00:08:16.780
Acosta also canceled the subpoenas,

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:18.510
which is highly problematic.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:20.540
From the time the FBI
started investigating

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:22.330
to the time of the agreement was struck,

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:23.800
the victims were never notified

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:25.910
about a potential
non-prosecution agreement,

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:28.670
nor were they ever told
that it was a possibility.

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:31.860
In possibly the most unbelievable
fact of this entire case

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:33.800
is that after the agreement was signed,

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:35.440
the government lawyers led by Acosta

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:37.240
started negotiating on
whether the government

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:41.540
would even comply with the Crime
Victims Right Act, or CVRA.

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:42.980
The purpose of the CVRA

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:45.940
is to keep victims in the
loop about the investigation,

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:48.030
and prosecution of criminal defendants.

00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:49.700
Certain victims have a right to know

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:51.920
what's going on with
the federal prosecution,

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:54.640
and it appears that both the DOJ lawyers,

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:55.810
and Epstein's lawyers

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:58.030
knew that there was a
compliance requirement.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:00.490
However, one of Epstein's
lawyers wrote an email

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:02.940
directing Acosta not to
have anyone from his office

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:05.010
reach out to the victims in any way.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:06.726
After this email, Acosta
then went out for breakfast

00:09:06.726 --> 00:09:08.990
with the Epstein lawyer

00:09:08.990 --> 00:09:10.550
where he promised that the government

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:12.900
would not in fact contact the victims.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:15.700
The agreement also gave
Epstein unprecedented control

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:18.260
over whether the victims
could sue him in civil court.

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:20.250
The agreement stipulated
that Epstein's attorneys

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.130
would be permitted to
select the civil lawyers

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:23.020
for each victim,

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:24.840
and an Epstein would pay those lawyers,

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:27.070
and that he would not contest liability.

00:09:27.070 --> 00:09:28.670
The whole purpose of these agreements

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:31.410
was to prevent any of the
information from becoming public.

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:33.670
Acosta also allowed
Epstein to stipulate that

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:34.650
paying off the victims

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:36.680
was not an admission of guilt whatsoever.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.107
Acosta also agreed that if
anyone requested public records

00:09:39.107 --> 00:09:42.228
under the state, or Federal
Freedom of Information Acts,

00:09:42.228 --> 00:09:44.430
the government would notify Epstein

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:46.770
before making the required disclosures.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:49.080
Thus, the deal made sure
that Epstein's lawyers

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:51.770
were always completely
informed of what was going on,

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:54.600
while the victims were
completely in the dark,

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:57.060
Epstein wasn't put in jail
in the traditional sense.

00:09:57.060 --> 00:09:59.300
He spent his nights in a Florida jail,

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:01.310
but during the day he was on work release

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:03.440
where his private driver
picked him up each day,

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:05.574
and drove him to his office downtown

00:10:05.574 --> 00:10:08.270
where Epstein was able
to visit with friends,

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:10.070
and colleagues for 12 hours a day.

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:12.490
Meanwhile, the victims
were waging a legal battle

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:14.290
to have the plea agreement unsealed.

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:18.200
Epstein was released from jail
five months early in 2009.

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:20.758
Although Epstein's probation
prohibited him from travel,

00:10:20.758 --> 00:10:22.720
the Miami Herald reports that Epstein

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.670
regularly traveled between
Florida, Manhattan,

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:26.130
and the U.S. Virgin Islands.

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:27.270
I probably don't need to tell you

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:29.080
that this is highly irregular.

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:30.770
If any other criminal
defendant had done this,

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:33.280
they would have been sentenced
for a probation violation,

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:35.180
but Epstein continued life unscathed,

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:37.470
even hanging out around
the beach in Florida

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:39.550
when he was supposed to be at the office.

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:42.200
Epstein's probation officer
said it was fine for Epstein

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:44.723
to walk around the beach when
he was supposed to be at work.

00:10:44.723 --> 00:10:46.990
He was allowed to get some exercise

00:10:46.990 --> 00:10:48.929
according to the probation officer.

00:10:48.929 --> 00:10:52.910
Additionally, Epstein failed
to register as a sex offender

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:54.850
as required by the plea deal,

00:10:54.850 --> 00:10:58.170
which again, if any other
criminal defendant had done that,

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:01.410
they would have been subject
to a probation violation.

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:03.710
By late 2009 dozens of victims

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:06.420
had filed civil lawsuits against Epstein.

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:09.570
Meanwhile, Epstein's ex
butler, Alfredo Rodriguez,

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:11.510
had possession of
Epstein's little black book

00:11:11.510 --> 00:11:12.520
of important people,

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:14.430
and tried to sell it to enrich himself.

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:16.640
Rodriguez was charged with
obstruction of justice

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:18.372
for not giving the black book to police.

00:11:18.372 --> 00:11:22.030
He served federal prison
time, and died in 2015.

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:24.830
Now, convicted sex offenders
are required to register

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:26.560
in any jurisdiction where they live.

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:29.080
Enter Manhattan district
attorney Cy Vance.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:31.350
You may have heard of Cy Vance
for his questionable handling

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:33.238
of high-profile sexual assault cases,

00:11:33.238 --> 00:11:35.970
including allegations
against Harvey Weinstein.

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:38.370
But in 2010 a prosecutor
from Vance's office

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:39.790
appeared in New York State Court

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:42.230
to argue that Epstein's
sex offender classification

00:11:42.230 --> 00:11:44.270
should be reduced to a lower level

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:45.980
so that he would have more freedom.

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:47.959
I've never heard of this happening before.

00:11:47.959 --> 00:11:50.850
Prosecutors are not in the
habit of telling judges

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:53.500
to help sex offenders get
a lower classification

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:56.170
to crimes they have already
admitted to committing.

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:58.600
Just listen to what the judge had to say.

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:00.637
Quote, "I have never seen
the prosecutor's office

00:12:00.637 --> 00:12:01.687
"do anything like this.

00:12:01.687 --> 00:12:04.947
"I have done many cases, much
less troubling than this one,

00:12:04.947 --> 00:12:06.277
"where prosecutors would never

00:12:06.277 --> 00:12:08.710
"make a downward argument like this."

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:10.610
Vance's office claims that one prosecutor

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:11.590
made a rookie mistake,

00:12:11.590 --> 00:12:14.200
and that he didn't even know
that Epstein was appearing

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:15.220
in New York court

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:17.920
to argue about his sex
offender classification,

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:20.390
but that probably doesn't
make a whole lot of sense.

00:12:20.390 --> 00:12:23.170
By this point in 2010
Epstein was a billionaire

00:12:23.170 --> 00:12:26.210
whose escapades had received
considerable press attention.

00:12:26.210 --> 00:12:28.507
Epstein tried to rehabilitate
his image in 2011,

00:12:28.507 --> 00:12:30.840
and 2012 by donating large sums of money,

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:32.650
and waging a PR campaign.

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:35.160
However, in 2012 a woman
named Virginia Roberts

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:37.320
alleged that she was forced
to have sex with lawyer

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:39.640
Alan Dershowitz, and Prince Andrew,

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:41.260
although victims, and alleged victims

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:43.160
continued to file civil lawsuits,

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:45.960
and fight for the Florida
indictment to be unsealed,

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:48.870
in 2016 Donald Trump
was elected president.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:51.210
His connections to Epstein
made mild headlines

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:52.760
in June of 2016 when a woman

00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:54.730
going by the name of Katie Johnson

00:12:54.730 --> 00:12:56.530
said that the president had raped her

00:12:56.530 --> 00:12:59.491
at a party at Epstein's mansion in 1994,

00:12:59.491 --> 00:13:02.140
when she was 13 years old at the time.

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:04.257
Trump, and Epstein deny those allegations,

00:13:04.257 --> 00:13:06.173
and the lawsuit never went anywhere.

00:13:06.173 --> 00:13:09.650
Because 11 days before
the election in 2016

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:11.310
Johnson dropped her lawsuit

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:13.320
alleging that she had been threatened.

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:16.050
Around the same time, shortly
after the inauguration,

00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:18.023
president Trump nominated Alex Acosta

00:13:18.023 --> 00:13:20.150
to lead the Department of Labor.

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:22.220
Although lawmakers
briefly questioned Acosta

00:13:22.220 --> 00:13:26.110
about the Epstein affair,
Acosta was confirmed.

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:27.940
Flash forward to today.

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:31.440
In 2019, victims finally won
an important court battle.

00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:33.880
The 2006 Florida indictment was unsealed,

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:35.680
revealing publicly for the first time,

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:37.640
how deeply involved in human trafficking

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:39.160
Epstein appeared to be.

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:41.550
Victims also won their lawsuit
alleging that Acosta's office

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:44.470
had violated the Crime Victims Rights Act

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:46.160
by failing to notify them.

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:48.140
Under the CVRA victims have a right

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:50.460
to be reasonably protected
from their assailants,

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:52.590
to be notified of any
public court hearings

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:53.910
in a timely fashion,

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:56.620
to be informed in a timely
manner of any plea bargain,

00:13:56.620 --> 00:13:58.680
or deferred prosecution agreement,

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:01.970
and to speak at any court
hearing involving a plea deal,

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:03.100
or sentencing.

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:06.220
Several victims sued in federal
court alleging that Acosta,

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:08.500
and the DOJ had failed to follow this law

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:09.560
by keeping them in the dark

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:12.240
about how the case with
Epstein had progressed.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:13.600
Now, under the CVRA,

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:16.430
a victim may make a
motion to reopen a plea,

00:14:16.430 --> 00:14:19.740
or sentence only if the
victim has asserted the right

00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:22.800
to be heard before, or during
the proceeding at issue,

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:24.510
and such right was denied,

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:26.740
the victim petitions the court of appeals

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:28.677
for writ of Mandamus within 14 days,

00:14:28.677 --> 00:14:30.620
and in a case of a plea,

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:33.730
the accused has not pled to
the highest offense charged.

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:35.910
The Federal District Court
judge ruled the prosecutors

00:14:35.910 --> 00:14:39.500
had violated the CVR by not
letting the more than 30

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:41.700
identified victims know of the deal

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:43.760
so that they could have
a chance to oppose it.

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:45.180
The judge rule that the government gave

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:47.530
deliberately misleading
information to victims,

00:14:47.530 --> 00:14:49.040
and promised Epstein's lawyers

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:52.060
not to notify the
victims of the plea deal.

00:14:52.060 --> 00:14:52.893
The judge rule that the government

00:14:52.893 --> 00:14:55.370
led the victims to believe
that the investigation,

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:56.770
and prosecution was ongoing,

00:14:56.770 --> 00:14:58.970
when in fact the
agreement had been signed,

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:01.400
and Epstein had already been sentenced.

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:03.770
However, the judge did
not reopen the plea deal.

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:05.950
Instead, he gave the
Department of Justice 15 days

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:07.800
to come up with a settlement proposal.

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:09.890
The DOJ argue that there was nothing wrong

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:12.060
with how Acosta handled the case.

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:14.130
It's against this legal backdrop

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:15.730
that prosecutors in New York

00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:18.110
are taking aim at Epstein once again,

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:19.210
the U.S. Attorney's Office

00:15:19.210 --> 00:15:20.560
for the Southern District of New York

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:23.430
charged Epstein recently
with child sex trafficking

00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:26.008
in violation of 18 U.S.C 1591,

00:15:26.008 --> 00:15:28.090
which outlaws sex trafficking activities

00:15:28.090 --> 00:15:30.320
that affect interstate,
or foreign commerce.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:31.660
The new indictment refers back

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:33.250
to the allegations in Florida, New York,

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:34.920
and New Mexico that were the subject

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:36.690
of the earlier agreement,

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:37.968
and now, although those events happened

00:15:37.968 --> 00:15:40.478
between 2002, and 2006,

00:15:40.478 --> 00:15:42.820
there was no longer a
statute of limitations

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:44.212
for child trafficking cases.

00:15:44.212 --> 00:15:47.730
The statute of limitations
was originally five years,

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:50.880
but before Epstein's statute
of limitations had run,

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:52.700
lawmakers changed the rule so

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:55.100
that there was no longer
a statute of limitations

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:56.730
for these particular cases,

00:15:56.730 --> 00:15:59.290
which means that Epstein
will not be protected

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:01.670
by any effective statute of limitations.

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:05.120
Now, whether Epstein's original
plea deal will protect him,

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:08.660
and give him immunity is
a bit of an open question.

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:10.620
Normal practice is to
include a clause saying,

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:13.160
and only binds the local
U.S. Attorney's Office,

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:14.630
which signed the agreement,

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:16.770
not any of the other
U.S. Attorney's Offices,

00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:19.010
which may seek to press charges,

00:16:19.010 --> 00:16:21.270
but the plea agreement drafted by Acosta

00:16:21.270 --> 00:16:23.330
does not include this clause.

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:27.250
This is of course, incredibly
unusual, and highly irregular,

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:29.700
although Epstein's lawyers
will surely try to argue

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:31.340
from this broad language that the entire

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:33.391
federal justice system
cannot prosecute Epstein

00:16:33.391 --> 00:16:36.820
for the conduct occurring in
Florida in the early 2000s,

00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:39.060
there's other language
in the plea agreement,

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:41.670
which more specifically
says the prosecution

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:44.310
cannot take place in a
specific federal district.

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:46.970
If this particular plea
agreement is litigated,

00:16:46.970 --> 00:16:49.360
it's very likely that a
judge would find in favor

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:50.630
of the Department of Justice,

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:53.570
and find that this plea
agreement does not bind

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:55.240
every other U.S. district.

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:57.520
Epstein's alleged crimes
took place in New York

00:16:57.520 --> 00:16:58.353
as well as Florida,

00:16:58.353 --> 00:17:00.250
so federal prosecutors
in the New York district

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:02.290
probably have the right
to prosecute Epstein

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:05.400
for the conduct that
occurred in that district.

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:08.180
As for concerns that
prosecution on old allegations

00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:10.331
violate the double jeopardy
clause of the U.S. constitution,

00:17:10.331 --> 00:17:12.950
the new indictment
apparently includes crimes

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:15.360
which were not charged in the older case,

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:18.850
including Epstein bringing
victims across state lines.

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:21.030
There are also new factual allegations

00:17:21.030 --> 00:17:22.280
against Epstein as well.

00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:25.040
When the government searched
Epstein's New York home,

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:27.330
they allegedly seized
hundreds of photographs

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:29.040
of nude under range girls.

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:31.090
The photos were kept on several CDs,

00:17:31.090 --> 00:17:34.224
with labels such as girl picks nude.

00:17:34.224 --> 00:17:36.150
That's something that's so on the nose,

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:38.060
you're not even going to
see that in an episode

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:39.850
of Law &amp; Order SVU,

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:42.320
but that's what happens
when a criminal defendant

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:44.130
thinks that they are
immune from prosecution

00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:45.430
for the rest of their lives.

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:46.610
So what happens next?

00:17:46.610 --> 00:17:49.320
Well, there are a number
of unanswered questions.

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:51.090
The first of which is
what's going to happen

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:53.820
to Jeffrey Epstein in the new prosecution

00:17:53.820 --> 00:17:55.640
in the southern district of New York.

00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:58.860
Will the courts allow the old plea deal

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:00.380
to provide any kind of immunity,

00:18:00.380 --> 00:18:02.610
or will they just simply throw it out?

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:05.500
Additionally, we don't
know what the remedy

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:07.439
for a violation of the CVRA is.

00:18:07.439 --> 00:18:10.237
Does that undo the plea agreement itself?

00:18:10.237 --> 00:18:13.520
Meanwhile, Acosta has
argued that the evidence

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:15.920
wasn't particularly strong at the time,

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:18.750
and that the Miami
prosecutors had said that

00:18:18.750 --> 00:18:22.270
if the DOJ didn't get an
admission of guilt from Epstein,

00:18:22.270 --> 00:18:25.960
that the prosecutors were simply
going to let Epstein walk.

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:28.680
So having the DOJ get the
plea agreement that they did

00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:31.220
with jail time was better
than nothing at all.

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:32.630
But one thing is for certain,

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:35.963
Alex Acosta is now out of a job after

00:18:35.963 --> 00:18:37.570
a press conference where
he heaps blame on victims,

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:38.840
and local Miami prosecutors

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:40.964
for the Epstein non-prosecution agreement.

00:18:40.964 --> 00:18:45.260
- Simply put, the Palm Beach
State Attorney's Office

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:47.710
was ready to let Epstein walk free.

00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:50.320
No jail time, nothing.

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:52.130
Without the work of our prosecutors,

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:57.130
Epstein would have gotten away
with just that state charge,

00:18:57.460 --> 00:18:59.453
and as to message the victims,

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:03.320
the message is you need to come forward.

00:19:03.320 --> 00:19:05.950
- The writing was on the
wall, and Acosta had to go,

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:09.440
Acosta resigned and President
Trump defended him, stating--

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:10.688
- Do you know what I know about Alex?

00:19:10.688 --> 00:19:13.760
He was a great student at Harvard.

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:17.320
He's Hispanic, which I so admire,

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:19.550
because maybe it was a
little tougher for him,

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:20.865
and maybe not,

00:19:20.865 --> 00:19:25.865
but he did an unbelievable
job as the Secretary of Labor.

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:27.570
That's what I know about him.

00:19:27.570 --> 00:19:28.772
I know one thing,

00:19:28.772 --> 00:19:32.019
he did a great job,
and until this came up,

00:19:32.019 --> 00:19:37.019
there was never an out the
problem with this very good man.

